What was the role of Rose Mary Woods and H. R. Haldeman in the administration of President Richard Nixon?
Based on the provided context, Rose Mary Woods was Richard Nixon's secretary from his days in Congress in 1951, through the end of his political career, serving as his gatekeeper before H. R. Haldeman and John Ehrlichman took over.

H. R. Haldeman, on the other hand, was the White House Chief of Staff to President Richard Nixon, and he, along with John Ehrlichman, were referred to as "the Berlin Wall" due to their reputation as stern taskmasters who protected Nixon's best interests and filtered information that came into his office.
