What are the historical or legislative reasons behind the differences in trade laws between Chennai and the rest of the country?
The historical and legislative reasons behind the differences in trade laws between Chennai and the rest of the country are primarily due to the process of legislative harmonization within the Community, as mentioned in the context of the Common Agricultural Policy. The policy aims to remove all hidden legislative barriers to trade, which can create problems for anyone seeking to trade between countries. This includes regulations on permitted preservatives or food coloring, labelling regulations, use of hormones or other drugs in livestock intended for human consumption, and disease control, among others.
