Research the other individuals who were part of the Boren-McCurdy proposals
Based on the provided context, the individuals who were part of the Boren-McCurdy proposals, in addition to Senator David Boren and Representative Dave McCurdy, are:

1. Admiral Stansfield Turner, former DCI under President Carter, who recommended establishing an NID to oversee the IC.
2. Ray Cline, a former Deputy Director of the CIA, who recommended that the DCI be given cabinet rank and broad supervisory authorities over the IC.
3. James R. Schlesinger, a future DCI and Deputy OMB Director, who headed the effort to recommend changes in the IC's organization and considered the creation of an NID.
4. Herbert Hoover, former President and chair of the Commission on Organization of the Executive Branch of the Government, also known as the Second Hoover Commission, which recommended that management of the CIA be turned over to an “executive officer,” so that the DCI could focus attention on the IC.
