Based on the context, the identified term is "William Shakespeare". The notable aspects of the playwright's works related to this term include:

* Widely regarded as the greatest writer in the English language and the world's greatest dramatist.
* His extant works consist of approximately 39 plays, 154 sonnets, two long narrative poems, and a few other verses, some of uncertain authorship.
* His plays have been translated into every major living language and are performed more often than those of any other playwright.
* His works have been performed in outdoor festivals, such as Shakespeare in the Park, which aims to make theatre available to people of all walks of life.

These aspects highlight the significance and impact of Shakespeare's works on literature and theatre, as well as their enduring popularity and global reach.
